        "term": "Ring 0 vs Ring 3",
        "definition": "x86 processors enforce a privilege hierarchy called protection rings. Ring 3 (user space) runs application code with limited access to hardware. Ring 0 (kernel space) has unrestricted hardware access. Rootkits aim to place code in Ring 0 to control the entire system. The /dev/kmem write in this sample is a Ring 3 → Ring 0 escalation vector.",
